# Wiki link repair — PREPARED, NOT APPLIED
#
# Two links in the firestarter wiki pointed at github.com/henols/firestarter/blob/beta/…,
# which meant the FIRMWARE repo. After the slug claim that path is the project hub and both
# return HTTP 404 (verified). PROTOCOLS.md and PINOUTS.md live in firestarter_fw, where the
# repointed URLs return HTTP 200 (verified).
#
# The push to the wiki was denied in this session (external system write), so this patch is
# banked rather than applied. To apply:
#
#   git clone https://github.com/henols/firestarter.wiki.git
#   cd firestarter.wiki && git apply /path/to/193-wiki-link-repair.patch && git commit -am 'Repoint two firmware doc links at firestarter_fw' && git push
#
# The firestarter_prom/issues links elsewhere in the wiki are deliberately NOT touched:
# that slug redirects to the hub and still resolves.

diff --git a/Pin-Maps.md b/Pin-Maps.md
index 76ebf1b..192eb7b 100644
--- a/Pin-Maps.md
+++ b/Pin-Maps.md
@@ -381,7 +381,7 @@ not write.
 
 The shield's own wiring — which Arduino pin drives which RURP signal, and the
 control-register bits behind them — is in
-[PINOUTS.md](https://github.com/henols/firestarter/blob/beta/PINOUTS.md)
+[PINOUTS.md](https://github.com/henols/firestarter_fw/blob/beta/PINOUTS.md)
 in the firmware repository.
 
